Mmap: allow the mapped file to be replaced on Windows.

`Vfs::mount_host` memory-maps every file under a mounted directory, and the
Win32 mapping opened the file with `FILE_SHARE_READ` only. That denies any
later rename-into-place over the file: Windows refuses the replacement with
ERROR_ACCESS_DENIED while the mapping lives.

The editor mounts the asset sources for as long as a world is open, and the
normal Gothic layout keeps worlds under one (`_work/Data/Worlds/`). Saving over
the open world therefore failed for exactly the worlds a user edits, even
though nothing ever reads a world through the VFS — it is mapped for sitting in
a mounted directory.

Add `FILE_SHARE_DELETE`. The rename is then permitted; the existing mapping
keeps serving the bytes it already mapped, which is the same guarantee the
POSIX implementation gives, where renaming over an mmap'd file has always been
legal.

--- a/src/MmapWin32.cc
+++ b/src/MmapWin32.cc
@@ -15,7 +15,7 @@ namespace zenkit {
 
 		hFile = CreateFileW(path.c_str(),
 		                    GENERIC_READ,
-		                    FILE_SHARE_READ,
+		                    FILE_SHARE_READ | FILE_SHARE_DELETE,
 		                    nullptr,
 		                    OPEN_EXISTING,
 		                    FILE_ATTRIBUTE_NORMAL,
